; TODO 7 -- the SOA record. Every zone starts with one:
;
;   $ORIGIN lab.test.
;   $TTL 60
;   @   IN  SOA ns.lab.test. admin.lab.test. (
;               <serial> ; bump on every change
;               3600     ; refresh
;               600      ; retry
;               604800   ; expire
;               60 )     ; negative TTL
;
; The serial is the interesting field. Secondaries refuse to reload a zone whose
; serial did not increase - you have no secondaries, so nothing will punish you
; for forgetting, which is exactly why the habit has to come from the renderer.
; A date-based serial (2026090101) is the convention.
;
; TODO 8 -- an NS record. A zone with no NS is malformed even when it answers.
;
;   @   IN  NS  ns.lab.test.
;   ns  IN  A   {{ host_ip }}
;
